Let $a$ be the number of articles Meredith wrote on Monday.
On Monday, she wrote 5 articles. So $a = 5$.
On Tuesday, she wrote $\frac{2}{5}$ times more articles than on Monday.
The number of articles written on Tuesday is $5 + \frac{2}{5} \times 5 = 5 + 2 = 7$.
On Wednesday, she wrote twice the number of articles she wrote on Tuesday.
The number of articles written on Wednesday is $2 \times 7 = 14$.
Total number of articles written in the three days is $5 + 7 + 14 = 26$.
A blog article takes an average of 4 hours to research and write.
The total number of hours she spent writing articles is $26 \times 4 = 104$.

The number of articles she wrote on Monday is 5.
The number of articles she wrote on Tuesday is $5 \times \frac{2}{5} = 2$. This means she wrote $5+2=7$ articles.
The number of articles she wrote on Wednesday is $2 \times 7 = 14$.
Total number of articles written = $5 + 7 + 14 = 26$ articles.
Since each article takes 4 hours, the total hours is $26 \times 4 = 104$.

